    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d29">

                <pb facs="0039" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1943v06/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Colombia/481: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-25T18:00:00-05:00">January 25, 1943—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>159. With reference to paragraph 2 of my telegram “No. 151<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d29-f1"/> and <pb facs="0040" n="26" xml:id="pg26"/> my telephone
                    conversation with Cissel<anchor n="54" xml:id="d29-f2"/> today, we suggest that
                    a redraft of paragraph 2–<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>, which was suggested as
                    an alternative by Urdaneta, be considered: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Rubber Reserve will be able to develop its activities, in the same
                            manner as Caja, in all production zones, but it must inform the
                            Commission in advance of the zones in which it intends to carry on its
                            work. The Government will authorize the respective licenses.[”]<anchor
                                n="55" xml:id="d29-f3"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d29-f1" n="53" xml:id="d29-f1-content">
                <p>Dated January 23, noon, <ref target="#pg21">p. 21</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d29-f2" n="54" xml:id="d29-f2-content">
                <p>T. Ross Cissel, Assistant Chief, Division of Defense Materials of the Department
                    of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d29-f3" n="55" xml:id="d29-f3-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 113, January 27, 1943, to the Ambassador in Colombia, the
                    Department stated that it was satisfied with this alternative. (811.20
                    Defense(M)Colombia 481).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
